{"agent_mode": null, "bash_calls": 3, "candidate_provenance": null, "cell_seed": 6406056413800506743, "checker_exit": 0, "checker_stderr": "", "checker_stdout": "round_money rounds half up; other helpers intact\nOBENCH_VERDICT: pass\n", "checker_workspace_files": {"pricing/__init__.py": {"bytes": 0, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"}, "pricing/money.py": {"bytes": 659, "mtime": 1791865359.9069886, "sha256": "a5ffbb169ccd10292b608d2816e59319b971c0ebe7eba297c993938b4ef81bf6"}, "tests/test_round_money.py": {"bytes": 385, "mtime": 1791865363.9111607, "sha256": "77f4c0903463e537723f9ca60b24c1df9a5458b9379cf6cfeec03e1e512b656b"}, "tests/test_split.py": {"bytes": 101, "mtime": 1791845574.119196, "sha256": "f21bbe9cf15cf7f51ff9f71318aca4794c29f5d66cb9ae2aa0d4c919043d9bcf"}}, "child_edit_calls": 0, "child_plan_reminder": false, "cmd": ["/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp", "-p", "`round_money(2.675)` returns `2.67` but customers expect `2.68`. Fix it.\n", "--mode", "json", "--provider", "vertex-anthropic", "--model", "claude-opus-5-5", "--yolo", "--session-dir", "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-38/omp-38/transcripts/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/3/session"], "completed": true, "dotnet_build_calls": 0, "edit_calls": 2, "ended_on_rejection": false, "error": null, "exec_mode": "local", "failure_class": "solved", "failure_reason": null, "faults_served": 0, "final_answer_complete": true, "final_answer_present": true, "final_answer_source": "json", "final_workspace": "/workspace/openbench-ab/results/omp-screen5-b2/omp-38/omp-38/cells/with/trig-omp-bugfix-regress/3/workspace", "fresh_subagents": 0, "harness": "omp", "harness_version": "omp/18.1.8 (/workspace/pi-check/cache5/bin/omp/1b5c7b53d2c460b2ede60d78591b6826facf0e4d/omp)", "harness_version_source": "host", "host": "grok-bot-vm-412615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test alongside the existing one.\nFixed: `round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, so the old `round(x, 2)` in `pricing/money.py` rounded it down. `round()` also rounds exact halves to the even digit (`round(0.125, 2)` gives `0.12`), which contradicts the \"half up\" promise in the function's docstring.\n\n**Fix:** `round_money` now converts the value to a `Decimal` using its shortest exact text form (`repr(2.675)` is `\"2.675\"`), then rounds to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP` and returns a float. `add_vat` uses `round_money`, so it gets the fix too.\n\n**Regression test:** I added `tests/test_round_money.py`. It checks `2.675 \u2192 2.68`, `0.125 \u2192 0.13`, `1.005 \u2192 1.01`, `2.674 \u2192 2.67`, `-2.675 \u2192 -2.68` and `10 \u2192 10.0`.\n- pytest isn't installed here, so I ran the new test and the existing `test_split` by calling them directly with python3. Both pass.\n- I didn't run the new test against the old code (there's no git repo to revert to). Instead I checked that the old `round()` gives `2.67`, `0.12` and `1.0` for the first three cases, so the test would have failed before the fix.\n\nTwo side effects:\n- Negative values round away from zero (`-2.675 \u2192 -2.68`). That is what `ROUND_HALF_UP` does, and what the test now expects.\n- The `Decimal` conversion is slower than plain `round()`. This only matters if prices are rounded in a hot loop.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 8, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 186609, "requests_cache_write": 45304, "requests_cost_usd": 0.3087138, "requests_count": 8, "requests_input_uncached": 18, "requests_output": 2240, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "